From 858c1b79d24d67bcf137edcda4cfd94d0478d416 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:46:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: himax-hx8279, drm: bridge: samsung-dsim,
 drm/exynos: decon7: drop the wake-up diagnostics

Remove what patches 0093, 0094 and 0096 added for the wake-up campaign:
the prints in the panel prepare, enable, disable, unprepare and backlight
update, the ones along the DSIM bring-up and tear-down and on the DECON
side, and the two write-only module parameters that resent the display on
command and the init table on a live panel.

They did their job. The panel init is now byte identical to the vendor
table, the power sequencing follows the board file, the reset line is
really driven and the PLL runs at the vendor operating point; what is
left of the wake-up stripes, about one in sixty, has no counterpart in
the vendor code and these prints cannot say anything more about it. They
run on every screen off and on, and the parameters let anyone rewrite the
DriverIC configuration behind the driver's back, so they do not belong in
a kernel that is used every day.

The functional changes of those three patches, if any, stay: none of
0093, 0094 and 0096 changed behaviour, they only reported it.
